- autocomplete="email" / "current-password" are what password managers key off — keep those tokens when porting.
- Client constraints are UX only; the server does the real validation. Failure copy is deliberately generic so the form can't be used to enumerate accounts.
- No minlength on the password on purpose — login shouldn't enforce policy; that belongs to signup/reset.
- Dark mode comes free via prefers-color-scheme; all theme tokens are CSS variables at the top.

