Two notes worth knowing:
- Luhn nuance for scenario testing: decline cards like 4000 0000 0000 0002 PASS the form (checksum valid — correct, declines come from the issuer side, not your form). 4242 4242 4242 4241 gets caught client-side; if you ever want to exercise the processor-side incorrect_number path, comment the luhn check or flag it. Covered both behaviors in the driver already.
- Infra heads-up: Hermes' usual browser backend (camofox at :9377) isn't provisioned on this box — nothing running, no image. I verified with local Chrome via playwright-core instead (that fallback is baked into verify.cjs). If you want Hermes' browser tools live here: docker run -p 9377:9377 -e CAMOFOX_PORT=9377 jo-inc/camofox-browser, or npm start in a camofox checkout.

